.\" vt-headless(1) - the manual page for vt-headless.
.\" Every option in `vt-headless --help` and `vt-headless kermit` is described
.\" here; a test in crates/vt-headless/src/main.rs checks it.
.TH VT-HEADLESS 1 "September 2026" "veetee" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vt-headless \- veetee's emulator without a window: Kermit transfers, recordings and traces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vt-headless kermit receive
.RB [ \-\-into
.IR DIR ]
.I CONNECTION
.RI [ OPTION ...]
.br
.B vt-headless kermit send
.IR FILE ...
.I CONNECTION
.RI [ OPTION ...]
.br
.B vt-headless replay
.I FILE.vtrec
.RB [ \-\-golden
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-bless ]
.br
.B vt-headless run
.I SCRIPT
.RB [ \-\-golden
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-bless ]
.RB [ \-\-record
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B vt-headless trace
.RB [ \-\-7bit " | " \-\-8bit " | " \-\-no\-c1 " | " \-\-utf8 ]
.RB [ \-\-vt52 ]
.RI [ FILE ]
.br
.B vt-headless lat
.I INTERFACE
.RI [ SECONDS ]
.RB [ \-\-connect
.I NODE
.RB [ \-\-service
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-type
.IR TEXT ]]
.br
.B vt-headless
.BR \-v | \-\-version
.br
.B vt-headless
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vt-headless
runs the emulator at the heart of
.BR veetee (1)
with no window: to transfer files with Kermit from a script, to replay session recordings and
test scripts against the screens they should produce, and to look at what a host sends.
.SH KERMIT
.B vt-headless kermit
transfers files with the Kermit protocol over a connection, as
.BR veetee 's
Send File and Receive File do.
Start the other end first, with SEND or RECEIVE at the host's Kermit prompt.
.B vt-headless kermit
alone lists its options.
.TP
.BI "receive \fR[\fP\-\-into " DIR \fR]\fP
Receive what the host sends, into
.I DIR
(the current directory by default).
A received name is made safe and never overwrites a file:
.I LOGIN.COM;3
arrives as
.IR login.com ,
or
.I login.1.com
if that is taken.
.TP
.BI send " FILE..."
Send the files.
.PP
The connection is one of:
.TP
.BI \-\-command " COMMAND"
Run
.I COMMAND
on a pty, through
.BR "sh \-c" ;
for example
.BR "gkermit \-s notes.txt" .
.TP
.BI \-\-telnet " HOST\fR[\fP:PORT\fR]"
Telnet.
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh " \fR[\fPUSER@\fR]\fPHOST"
SSH, through the system's OpenSSH client.
.TP
.BI \-\-serial " DEVICE"
A serial line, with
.B \-b
.IR RATE ,
.B \-d
.IR BITS ,
.B \-p
.IR PARITY ,
.B \-s
.I STOP
and
.B \-f
.I FLOW
as for
.BR veetee (1).
With no window there is no Set-Up: what they leave out is DEC's factory setting, 9600 8N1 with
XON/XOFF.
.PP
The options:
.TP
.B \-\-binary
Send the bytes exactly.
The default is text, with CR LF on the line, and the host's Kermit is told which with attribute
packets where it takes them.
.TP
.B "\-\-names as\-sent"
Keep a received name as sent, version and case included.
.TP
.BR \-\-check " 1|2|3"
The block check to ask for: 3, the CRC, by default.
A Kermit that cannot do it answers otherwise, and both then use 1.
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " N"
Tries before giving up on a packet (10).
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print every packet to standard error.
.PP
The exit status is 0 when every file arrived, and 1 otherwise.
.SH REPLAY
.B vt-headless replay
plays a recording made with
.B veetee \-\-record
through the emulator and compares the screen at each checkpoint, and at the end as
.IR final ,
with the snapshots in
.I DIR
(by default, the recording's name without
.IR .vtrec ).
.TP
.BI \-\-golden " DIR"
Where the snapshots are.
.TP
.B \-\-bless
Write the snapshots from this replay, in place of comparing.
.SH RUN
.B vt-headless run
runs a session script against the emulator on a pty and compares its snapshots with
.IR DIR / NAME .screen.
.TP
.BI \-\-golden " DIR"
Where the snapshots are.
.TP
.B \-\-bless
Rewrite them.
.TP
.BI \-\-record " FILE"
Record the session as well.
.SH TRACE
.B vt-headless trace
prints each action the parser takes on
.I FILE
(standard input when there is none), one to a line.
.TP
.B \-\-7bit
A 7-bit line: the eighth bit of every byte is stripped.
.TP
.B \-\-8bit
An 8-bit line, the default: 0x80 to 0x9F are C1 controls and 0xA0 to 0xFF graphics.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-c1
An 8-bit line whose 0x80 to 0x9F are not controls, and are discarded.
.TP
.B \-\-utf8
UTF-8, whose encoded U+0080 to U+009F act as C1 controls.
.TP
.B \-\-vt52
The VT52's escape sequences.
.SH LAT
.B vt-headless lat
prints the LAT messages heard on
.I INTERFACE
for
.I SECONDS
(until interrupted, where there are none).
Linux only; it needs CAP_NET_RAW, since LAT is raw Ethernet rather than IP.
.TP
.BI \-\-connect " NODE"
Ask
.I NODE
for a circuit once it has announced itself, and open a session.
.TP
.BI \-\-service " NAME"
The service to ask for; by default, the node's own name.
.TP
.BI \-\-type " TEXT"
A line to send to the session.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of the commands and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B vt-headless kermit receive \-\-into ~/incoming \-\-telnet vms1
Receive what SEND at vms1's Kermit prompt sends.
.TP
.B vt-headless kermit send LOGIN.COM \-\-serial /dev/ttyUSB0 \-b 9600
Send a file down a serial line.
.TP
.B vt-headless replay edt\-keypad.vtrec
Check a recording's screens against its snapshots.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR veetee (1),
.BR kermit (1)
.PP
The wiki: https://github.com/issinoho/veetee/wiki
